    "viz_attribution": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### Attribution and third-party data\n\nWeather and geocoding data in live mode comes from [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com/) and is licensed under [CC BY 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/) — see their [license page](https://open-meteo.com/en/license).\n\nWind Compass is free, non-commercial, and not affiliated with Open-Meteo. It uses Open-Meteo's free API tier, which is rate-limited and for non-commercial use only ([terms of use](https://open-meteo.com/en/terms)). If you ship this as part of a commercial product, check whether you need a paid Open-Meteo plan. No Splunk data, credentials or API keys are ever sent to Open-Meteo. Full details are in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.",
        "backgroundColor": "transparent",
        "fontColor": "#d7e0ec",
        "fontSize": "small"
      }
    },
    "viz_dataflow_card": {
      "type": "splunk.rectangle",
      "options": {
        "fillColor": "#1e293e",
        "fillOpacity": 1,
        "strokeColor": "#77abee",
        "strokeOpacity": 0.7,
        "strokeWidth": 1.5,
        "rx": 14
      }
    },
    "viz_dataflow": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### Where live data comes from\n\n- Splunk serves the dashboard and the panel's code, then takes no further part: no search runs and nothing is indexed.\n- The **viewer's browser** asks Open-Meteo for the city's coordinates, then for current conditions, and draws the dial itself.\n- Requests come from each viewer's own browser, not from the Splunk server.\n- Only a city name and coordinates leave your network — no Splunk data, credentials or API keys.\n- Live readings are not stored, so they cannot be searched or alerted on. Use Search mode for that.",
        "backgroundColor": "transparent",
        "fontColor": "#e6ecf4",
        "fontSize": "small"
      }
    }
  },
